---
/**
 * Prototype of `view` (see docs/superpowers/specs/2026-11-19-view-design.md): a container shows the children whose `view`
 * matches its own. Kept as a reference, not part of the docs. No core changes — a small script below
 * plays the part the components would play, and the `.views` wrappers stand in
 * for what le-button would do inside its shadow DOM.
 */
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Lab: views">
  <main class="lab">
    <h1>view — prototype</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      A container has <code>view="…"</code>; children with <code>view="a b"</code> are shown in views <code>a</code> and
      <code>b</code>; children without it are always shown. The container decides <em>how</em> to switch:
      a button cross-fades (and is as large as its largest view), a block collapses (height animates, no measuring).
    </p>

    <div class="presets" data-presets>
      <span>Motion preset (on <code>&lt;html&gt;</code>, whole page):</span>
      {["none", "fade", "slide", "scale", "blur", "spring"].map((p) => (
        <le-button size="small" variant="outlined" selected={p === "fade"} data-preset={p}>{p}</le-button>
      ))}
    </div>

    <h2>1. Buttons — cross-fade, size of the largest view</h2>

    <div class="row">
      <le-button variant="outlined" view="idle" data-views data-copy>
        <span slot="icon-start" class="views">
          <le-icon name="copy" view="idle"></le-icon>
          <le-icon name="check" view="done"></le-icon>
        </span>
        <span class="views">
          <span view="idle">Copy</span>
          <span view="done" aria-live="polite">Copied</span>
        </span>
      </le-button>

      <le-button variant="solid" view="idle" data-views data-save>
        <span slot="icon-start" class="views">
          <le-icon name="save" view="idle"></le-icon>
          <span class="spinner" view="saving"></span>
          <le-icon name="check" view="saved"></le-icon>
        </span>
        <span class="views">
          <span view="idle">Save</span>
          <span view="saving">Saving…</span>
          <span view="saved" aria-live="polite">Saved</span>
        </span>
      </le-button>

      <le-button variant="filled" color="secondary" view="closed" data-views data-toggle>
        <le-icon slot="icon-start" name="chevron-down" class="chevron"></le-icon>
        <span class="views">
          <span view="closed">Show all 12 lines</span>
          <span view="open">Show less</span>
        </span>
      </le-button>

      <le-button variant="outlined" view="paused" data-views data-play>
        <span slot="icon-start" class="views">
          <le-icon name="play" view="paused"></le-icon>
          <le-icon name="pause" view="playing"></le-icon>
        </span>
        <span class="views">
          <span view="paused">Play</span>
          <span view="playing">Pause</span>
        </span>
      </le-button>
    </div>

    <p class="note">Same buttons in a narrow column — the text wraps the same way in every view, nothing jumps:</p>
    <div class="narrow" id="narrow"></div>

    <pre class="code">{`<le-button view="idle">
  <le-icon slot="icon-start" name="save" view="idle"></le-icon>
  <le-spinner slot="icon-start" view="saving"></le-spinner>
  <le-icon slot="icon-start" name="check" view="saved"></le-icon>
  <span view="idle">Save</span>
  <span view="saving">Saving…</span>
  <span view="saved" announce>Saved</span>
</le-button>

button.view = 'saving';`}</pre>

    <h2>2. A block — collapse, height animates</h2>
    <p class="note">Loading / empty / error / content. The leaving view collapses while the next one opens.</p>

    <div class="switch">
      {["loading", "empty", "error", "content"].map((v) => <le-button size="small" variant="clear" data-set-view={v}>{v}</le-button>)}
    </div>

    <div class="card" view="loading" data-views data-block>
      <h3>Recent orders</h3>
      <le-collapse view="loading">
        <div class="skeleton"><i></i><i></i><i></i></div>
      </le-collapse>
      <le-collapse view="empty" closed>
        <p class="muted">No orders yet.</p>
      </le-collapse>
      <le-collapse view="error" closed>
        <p class="error">Couldn't load orders. <a href="#">Try again</a></p>
      </le-collapse>
      <le-collapse view="content" closed>
        <ul>
          <li>#1042 — Desk lamp — €39</li>
          <li>#1041 — Notebook — €12</li>
          <li>#1040 — Fountain pen — €64</li>
          <li>#1039 — Ink, blue — €9</li>
        </ul>
      </le-collapse>
    </div>

    <h2>3. le-collapse as the same system — "Read more"</h2>
    <p class="note">
      The first paragraph has no <code>view</code> — always shown. The rest is <code>view="full"</code>. "Closed" is
      just the view where that part is absent; the toggle is the morphing button from section 1.
    </p>

    <div class="text" view="short" data-views data-readmore>
      <p>
        Le-kit components are built in layers: anatomy, styling, states, behavior, and only then motion. Each layer is
        approved before the next one is stacked on top of it.
      </p>
      <le-collapse view="full" closed>
        <p>
          The reason is simple: once actions and animations sit on a composition that doesn't feel right, it becomes
          hard to say what to change, and too costly to throw it away. So we stop after each layer, look at it, and
          only then move on.
        </p>
        <p>That is also why the docs site is the sandbox: every layer is visible on a real page.</p>
      </le-collapse>
      <le-button size="small" variant="clear" view="short" data-views data-readmore-toggle>
        <le-icon slot="icon-start" name="chevron-down" class="chevron"></le-icon>
        <span class="views">
          <span view="short">Read more</span>
          <span view="full">Show less</span>
        </span>
      </le-button>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>

<script>
  type Collapse = HTMLElement & { closed: boolean };

  /** The mechanic: show children whose `view` list contains the container's view. */
  function applyView(container: HTMLElement) {
    const current = (container.getAttribute("view") ?? "").split(/\s+/);
    container.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[view]").forEach((child) => {
      // Only this container's own children, not those of a nested container.
      if (child.parentElement?.closest("[data-views]") !== container) return;
      const on = child.getAttribute("view")!.split(/\s+/).some((v) => current.includes(v));
      if (child.tagName === "LE-COLLAPSE") {
        (child as Collapse).closed = !on;
      } else if (on && child.hasAttribute("data-off")) {
        // Entering starts from the enter point, not from where it left.
        child.setAttribute("data-enter", "");
        void child.offsetWidth;
        child.removeAttribute("data-off");
        child.removeAttribute("data-enter");
      } else if (!on) {
        child.setAttribute("data-off", "");
      }
    });
  }

  function setView(container: HTMLElement, view: string) {
    container.setAttribute("view", view);
    applyView(container);
  }

  // The narrow column gets copies of the four buttons.
  const narrow = document.getElementById("narrow")!;
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(".row > le-button").forEach((b) => narrow.append(b.cloneNode(true)));

  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-views]").forEach(applyView);

  // The preset lives on <html>, so it applies to everything on the page.
  const setPreset = (preset: string) => {
    document.documentElement.setAttribute("motion-preset", preset);
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-preset]").forEach((b) => {
      if (b.dataset.preset === preset) b.setAttribute("selected", "");
      else b.removeAttribute("selected");
    });
  };
  setPreset("fade");
  document.querySelector("[data-presets]")?.addEventListener("click", (e) => {
    const b = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLElement>("[data-preset]");
    if (b) setPreset(b.dataset.preset!);
  });

  const later = (ms: number) => new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, ms));

  document.addEventListener("click", async (event) => {
    const el = (event.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLElement>(
      "[data-copy], [data-save], [data-toggle], [data-play], [data-set-view], [data-readmore-toggle]",
    );
    if (!el) return;

    if (el.matches("[data-copy]")) {
      setView(el, "done");
      await later(1600);
      setView(el, "idle");
    } else if (el.matches("[data-save]")) {
      if (el.getAttribute("view") !== "idle") return;
      setView(el, "saving");
      el.setAttribute("disabled", "");
      await later(1400);
      el.removeAttribute("disabled");
      setView(el, "saved");
      await later(1600);
      setView(el, "idle");
    } else if (el.matches("[data-toggle]")) {
      setView(el, el.getAttribute("view") === "open" ? "closed" : "open");
    } else if (el.matches("[data-play]")) {
      setView(el, el.getAttribute("view") === "playing" ? "paused" : "playing");
    } else if (el.matches("[data-set-view]")) {
      setView(document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-block]")!, el.dataset.setView!);
    } else if (el.matches("[data-readmore-toggle]")) {
      const next = el.getAttribute("view") === "full" ? "short" : "full";
      setView(el, next);
      setView(el.closest<HTMLElement>("[data-readmore]")!, next);
    }
  });
</script>

<style>
  .lab {
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 2rem auto;
    padding: 0 1rem;
  }

  .lead,
  .note {
    opacity: 0.8;
  }

  .row {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: var(--le-spacing-3);
    align-items: center;
  }

  .narrow {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--le-spacing-2);
    width: 6.5rem;
    padding: var(--le-spacing-2);
    border: 1px dashed var(--le-color-border);
  }

  /* The cross-fade: every view in one grid cell, so the cell is as large as the
     largest view; inactive ones fade out and keep their place. */
  .views {
    display: grid;
    justify-items: center;
    align-items: center;
  }

  /* In the icon slot the wrapper stays inline (the slot is sized by the icon). */
  .views[slot] {
    display: inline-grid;
  }

  /* View motion tokens — a prototype of what would go to themes/base.css.
     Separate enter (where a view comes from) and exit (where it goes to). */
  :global(:root),
  :global([motion-preset="fade"]) {
    --le-motion-view-duration: 180ms;
    --le-motion-view-easing: ease;
    --le-motion-view-enter: none;
    --le-motion-view-exit: none;
    --le-motion-view-blur: 0px;
  }
  :global([motion-preset="none"]) {
    --le-motion-view-duration: 0ms;
    --le-collapse-duration: 0ms;
  }
  :global([motion-preset="slide"]) {
    --le-motion-view-duration: 220ms;
    --le-motion-view-easing: cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1);
    --le-motion-view-enter: translateY(0.7em);
    --le-motion-view-exit: translateY(-0.7em);
    --le-motion-view-blur: 0px;
  }
  :global([motion-preset="scale"]) {
    --le-motion-view-duration: 200ms;
    --le-motion-view-easing: cubic-bezier(0.2, 0, 0, 1);
    --le-motion-view-enter: scale(0.6);
    --le-motion-view-exit: scale(1.3);
    --le-motion-view-blur: 0px;
  }
  :global([motion-preset="blur"]) {
    --le-motion-view-duration: 260ms;
    --le-motion-view-easing: ease;
    --le-motion-view-enter: scale(0.97);
    --le-motion-view-exit: scale(1.03);
    --le-motion-view-blur: 6px;
  }
  :global([motion-preset="spring"]) {
    --le-motion-view-duration: 420ms;
    --le-motion-view-easing: cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1);
    --le-motion-view-enter: translateY(0.8em) scale(0.8);
    --le-motion-view-exit: translateY(-0.6em) scale(0.9);
    --le-motion-view-blur: 0px;
  }

  .views > [view] {
    grid-area: 1 / 1;
    --d: var(--le-motion-view-duration);
    --e: var(--le-motion-view-easing);
    transition:
      opacity var(--d) var(--e),
      transform var(--d) var(--e),
      filter var(--d) var(--e),
      visibility 0s;
  }

  .views > [data-off] {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: var(--le-motion-view-exit);
    filter: blur(var(--le-motion-view-blur));
    visibility: hidden;
    transition:
      opacity var(--d) var(--e),
      transform var(--d) var(--e),
      filter var(--d) var(--e),
      visibility 0s var(--d);
  }

  .views > [data-enter] {
    transform: var(--le-motion-view-enter);
    filter: blur(var(--le-motion-view-blur));
    transition: none;
  }

  /* One icon in both views: not swapped but turned. */
  .chevron {
    transition: rotate var(--le-motion-view-duration) var(--le-motion-view-easing);
  }

  [view="open"] > .chevron,
  [view="full"] > .chevron {
    rotate: 180deg;
  }

  .spinner {
    display: inline-block;
    width: 0.9em;
    height: 0.9em;
    border: 2px solid currentColor;
    border-right-color: transparent;
    border-radius: 50%;
    animation: spin 700ms linear infinite;
  }

  @keyframes spin {
    to {
      rotate: 360deg;
    }
  }

  .code {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
  }

  .presets {
    position: sticky;
    top: calc(var(--le-header-height, 0px) + var(--le-spacing-2));
    z-index: 5;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--le-spacing-1);
    padding: var(--le-spacing-2);
    border-radius: var(--le-radius-lg);
    background: var(--le-color-surface, #fff);
    box-shadow: var(--le-shadow-md);
  }

  .switch {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--le-spacing-1);
    margin-bottom: var(--le-spacing-2);
  }

  .card {
    max-width: 24rem;
    padding: var(--le-spacing-3) var(--le-spacing-4);
    border-radius: var(--le-radius-lg);
    background: var(--le-color-surface, #fff);
    box-shadow: var(--le-shadow-md);
  }

  .card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 var(--le-spacing-2);
    font-size: 1rem;
  }

  .card ul {
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.2em;
  }

  .skeleton {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--le-spacing-2);
    padding: var(--le-spacing-1) 0;
  }

  .skeleton i {
    height: 0.9em;
    border-radius: 4px;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--le-color-text, #000) 10%, transparent);
  }

  .skeleton i:nth-child(2) {
    width: 80%;
  }

  .skeleton i:nth-child(3) {
    width: 60%;
  }

  .muted {
    opacity: 0.7;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .error {
    color: var(--le-color-danger, #c0392b);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .text {
    max-width: 34rem;
  }
</style>
